# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Tina Torabi et al. (2026). Scalable data-driven basis selection for linear machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/ae49e2  arXiv:2504.16418v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2504.16418v2 (sha256 91df11c827b866c0...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 544 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/torabi2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: linear ACE models fitted with dense (RRQR, BLR) and
# sparse (ASP homotopy LASSO, OMP, ARD) solvers: small (about 300) and
# large (about 1000) basis models for the six single-element datasets of
# Zuo et al. (Ni, Cu, Li, Mo, Si, Ge; Table 2) and OMP/BLR models for a
# liquid-water dataset (Table 6). Test MAEs as printed. Literature MTP,
# GAP and CACE values, the silicon (PRX 2018) property comparisons and
# diffusivities are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
